Package: sonicray
Type: Package
Title: Hardware-Accelerated Metal Ray Tracing, Light-Layer Relighting, and Audio-Visual Synchronization
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Matthew", "Ross", email = "matthew.r.v.ross@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: A next-generation GPU rendering and relighting engine for R on Apple Silicon
    (Metal 3 hardware ray tracing + Intel Open Image Denoise), designed as a 10x-25x faster
    evolution of the rayshader/rayrender workflow for large-scale 3D environmental data films.
    Inspired by, and an attempt to follow, the work of Tyler Morgan-Wall (rayshader, rayrender); not
    affiliated with or endorsed by him and containing none of his code.
    Keeps terrain meshes and 4K/8K textures resident in unified GPU memory across hundreds of
    light layers, evaluates Next-Event Estimation (NEE) across multiple lights per BVH traversal,
    denoises with OIDN using first-hit albedo/normal AOVs, and compiles declarative timelines
    simultaneously to a GPU linear light-layer compositor and frame-accurate Sonic Pi scores.
